<div id="speaking-app" class="studio">
  <div class="studio-heading"><span class="eyebrow">LISTEN · NOTICE · SAY IT AGAIN</span><h2>A small pronunciation atelier.</h2><p>Hear a model, record your version, then compare. Work on one feature at a time: vowels, rhythm, liaison, or a clear message.</p></div>
  <label>Stage<select id="speak-stage">{Array.from({length:10},(_,i)=><option value={i+1}>Stage {i+1}</option>)}</select></label>
  <label>Model phrase<textarea id="speak-target" lang="fr" rows="3">Bonjour, je voudrais apprendre le français.</textarea></label>
  <div class="control-grid"><label>French voice<select id="speak-voice"><option value="">Waiting for installed voices…</option></select></label><label>Playback speed<select id="speak-rate"><option value="0.7">Careful · 0.7</option><option value="0.9" selected>Natural · 0.9</option><option value="1">Normal · 1.0</option></select></label></div>
  <div class="button-row"><button id="speak-model" class="primary">▶ Hear the model</button><button id="speak-next">Another phrase</button><button id="speak-stop">Stop playback</button></div>
  <p class="small-note">Voices are synthetic. “French” describes the voice’s language setting, not a guarantee of a human native recording. A voice marked online may use your device provider’s service.</p>
  <h3>Record and listen back</h3><p>Record up to 30 seconds. Your recording stays in this page and is discarded when you leave. Microphone permission is requested only when you start.</p>
  <div class="button-row"><button id="record-start">● Record my voice</button><button id="record-stop" disabled>■ Finish recording</button></div><audio id="record-player" controls hidden aria-label="Your speaking recording"></audio>
  <h3>On-device speech recognition</h3><p>Use a French language pack to turn your speech into editable text locally. If local French recognition is unavailable, use recording and self-review.</p><div class="button-row"><button id="recognition-check">Check local French support</button><button id="recognition-install" hidden>Download French speech pack</button><button id="recognition-start" disabled>Start local dictation</button><button id="recognition-stop" disabled>Stop dictation</button></div>
  <label>Your French transcript<textarea id="speak-transcript" lang="fr" rows="4" placeholder="Your local transcript appears here. You can also type it yourself."></textarea></label>
  <button id="compare-transcript">Compare words with model</button><p id="comparison-result" role="status"></p>
  <h3>Optional Chrome on-device AI coach</h3><p>On supported desktop Chrome devices, the coach can give tentative feedback on your French transcript or recorded audio. Enabling it may download a large browser-managed model. Availability depends on the browser, hardware, language, and audio support.</p>
  <div class="button-row"><button id="ai-enable">Enable on-device coach</button><button id="ai-text" disabled>Discuss my transcript</button><button id="ai-audio" disabled>Discuss my recording</button><button id="ai-cancel" disabled>Cancel feedback</button><button id="ai-reset" disabled>Unload coach session</button></div>
  <pre id="ai-feedback" class="ai-feedback" aria-live="polite"></pre>
  <p id="speak-status" role="status">Ready. Choose a French phrase.</p>
  <details><summary>A better self-review than a single score</summary><ol><li>Can a listener understand the intended message without reading it?</li><li>Are /y/ and /u/, oral and nasal vowels, and meaningful consonants distinct?</li><li>Do phrase groups flow without stressing every word?</li><li>Can you repair a misunderstanding or rephrase without abandoning the message?</li><li>At B2–C1, is your explanation organized, nuanced, and appropriate to the audience?</li></ol><p>Word matching measures transcript overlap. It does not measure accent, intonation, fluency, or CEFR level. Ask a proficient French speaker for periodic feedback. AI advice can be mistaken.</p></details>
</div>
<script>import '../scripts/speaking';</script>
